NOT-A-SECRET. This file is bait for the ETHR web-server canary.

If you can read this over HTTP, <FilesMatch>/Require all denied is not being
enforced on this host.

Read secret.env.probe before concluding anything about the deployment. THAT is
the bait blocked by `RewriteRule ... [F,L]`, which is the mechanism the
shared-hosting .htaccess actually uses; this one tests an authorization grant
the deployment does not rely on. The two can legitimately disagree.

The remediation this file used to give — "route the equivalent rules through
the Plesk nginx 'Additional directives' panel instead" — is WITHDRAWN. That
field does not exist on this plan (G0-A, read twice), and
deployment/SHARED-HOSTING-CONTRACT.md forbids requiring it. GATE-0-RESULT.md
carries the exact coverage a G0-B.3 failure leaves, which is not the same as
"there is a workaround".

Nothing here is confidential.
